From 08227ec7db58caf5e82471914325f51f96600369 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 03:39:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Sync the axiom audit file with CI, drop the dead certificate
 import, narrow the shard trigger

- Erdos302/Axioms.lean now audits the five endpoint declarations that the
  integration workflow checks, instead of a stale list that omitted the final
  theorem; the workflow runs this file rather than a heredoc copy.
- Erdos302.lean no longer imports Erdos302.Generated.PackingCertificates: the
  rational trace family is not reachable from the final theorem, so the
  default lake target stops compiling about 2,500 unused modules.
- packing-ci-canary.yml triggers only on files the certificate shards import,
  instead of every Lean file under Erdos302/.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VstGbUBvQMgh9AEzEKDvMz
